## Control {{controlId}}: Protect the Confidentiality of Backup CUI at Storage Locations

**Implementation Status:** {{status}}

This organization protects backup CUI at storage locations within the {{tenantName}} M365 GCC High tenant through encrypted cloud storage, access controls, and backup procedures documented in "Backup Protection Policy v1.0" maintained by {{variables.systemAdministrator}}.

**Cloud Backup Protection:**
M365 GCC High provides built-in backup and retention protections for CUI:
- **Exchange Online:** Mailbox data backed up with 14-day retention (recoverable items), encrypted at rest with AES-256
- **SharePoint Online / OneDrive:** Version history and recycle bin provide 93-day recovery; site-level backup with encryption
- **Teams:** Chat and channel data retained per compliance retention policies

{{#if bitLockerEnforced}}
**Endpoint Backup Encryption:**
{{deviceCount}} managed devices with BitLocker encryption ensure local backups are cryptographically protected. Recovery keys stored securely in Entra ID.
{{/if}}

{{#if dlpLabelsConfigured}}
**Label-Protected Backups:**
Sensitivity labels persist through backup and restore operations, maintaining CUI access restrictions on restored content.
{{/if}}

**Backup Access Controls:**
- Backup storage access restricted to designated backup administrators via RBAC
- Backup data inherits the same classification and access restrictions as source data
- Backup restoration requires authorization from {{variables.systemAdministrator}}
- Backup media stored in geographically separated Microsoft-managed datacenters within US sovereign boundary

**Responsible Party:** {{variables.systemAdministrator}}

**Verification Method:** Examine M365 retention policies, backup encryption configurations, RBAC assignments for backup access, and backup restoration authorization records.

